Components adapted, as they exist in THIS repository:

1. The agent persona — `packages/agent/src/context/instructions.ts`. Derived from the Codex
   terminal-agent persona (`codex-rs/core/gpt_5_codex_prompt.md`). It is a derivative work,
   not a verbatim copy: the behavioural discipline (when to plan and when to just act, editing
   constraints, review mindset, concise `file:line`-referenced answers) is re-expressed against
   this product's own tool surface. The file declares the derivation on its second line.

2. The `usage` shape of the headless JSON protocol — `packages/cli/src/runtime/events.ts`
   (`toCodexUsage`). The event names and the token-accounting fields follow Codex's wire format
   so that a consumer written against Codex reads this output without translation.

3. The tool contract — the names the model is trained on are Codex's. Measured in this tree:
   `run_shell` and `apply_patch` (`packages/agent/src/tools/registry.ts`), `edit_file` and
   `read_file` (`packages/agent/src/chat.ts`), and `update_plan`, `write_stdin`, `web_search`,
   `interactive_shell` as rendered contracts in `packages/tui/src/formatting/tool-header.ts`.
   They are a contract with the model: diverging from them would cost behaviour, not gain
   independence.

4. The command and posture vocabulary — `/compact`, `/review`, `/goal`, `/fork`, `/archive`,
   the three approval modes and the three sandbox modes follow Codex's semantics.

Attribution is retained per Apache-2.0 § 4(d).

NOTE ON SCOPE (2026-08-07): the NOTICE of the repository this code was extracted from also lists
a patch-application sequence search and a cBPF seccomp filter as adapted components. Both were
measured as absent from this tree — they now live in the `@theokit/agents` SDK, which is consumed
here as a dependency and carries its own attribution. Listing them here would claim a derivation
this repository does not distribute.

